From 2a54ee83e96ce757a802e4c6869348ad3d8fc7a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:27:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plugins): update ZIP dependency past extraction
 advisories

ZIP 2.4.2 fails the maintained dependency audit for RUSTSEC-2026-0367,
RUSTSEC-2026-0368, and RUSTSEC-2026-0369. Select ZIP 9.0.4, adapt the
archive reader API, and refresh Cargo and Bazel dependency metadata.

Allow the bzip2 license only for the replacement libbz2-rs-sys backend;
its redistribution conditions match the bundled libbzip2 it replaces.
Retain ZIP default compression features and all advisory checks.

Rebase the Windows zstd-sys header overlay onto the upgraded dependency.
Its target_is_msvc helper already handles symbol visibility, so retain
only the header search paths that remain necessary.

Red: CI 39019780120 job 117359126898 rejects ZIP 2.4.2 for all three
advisories. The local full audit additionally rejects libbz2-rs-sys
before its crate-specific license allowance.
Green: cargo deny --manifest-path codex-rs/Cargo.toml --all-features
check --deny unmatched-source --deny license-not-encountered
--deny unused-wrapper --deny advisory-not-detected passes.
just test -p codex-core-plugins: 478 passed, zero skipped.
just fmt-check and just bazel-lock-check pass.

Bazel dependency analysis reproduces the stale overlay failure and passes
with the narrowed overlay; no compile result is inferred from analysis.
Fresh emitted queue: exact tree equality, 478 plugin tests, formatting,
full audit, and lock verification pass.

This is an intermediate source checkpoint. Fresh emitted-patch and
hosted platform verification remain required before promotion.
---
